/ A loop's item is the loop's own: inside the body it is each element, after the loop it is gone.
Start
- set %names% = ["a", "b"]
- foreach %names%, call Remember
- assert %last% equals "b", "inside the body the item is each element"
- assert %item% is null, "the loop's item ends with the loop"

Remember
- set %last% = %item%
